# Release scan exceptions (R1-45).
#
# The release gate (.github/workflows/release.yml, job `scan`) scans the amd64 AND the arm64 image by digest and
# fails on ANY CRITICAL finding, including findings that have no fix yet. There is no blanket `ignore-unfixed`:
# an unfixed CRITICAL is either waited out or recorded here, visibly, in the commit history of this file.
#
# Every exception is two lines and nothing else:
#
#   # reason: <why this finding does not affect Whiskers or cannot be fixed yet; who decided; link/issue>
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN exp:YYYY-MM-DD
#
# `exp:` is the review date. Trivy stops ignoring the entry after that date, so the next release fails again
# until someone re-checks the finding and either removes the entry or renews it with a new reason.
# ReleaseWorkflowTests rejects entries without a reason line or without an expiry date.
#
# No exceptions are recorded.
